<Layout title="Projects" schema={{'@context':'https://schema.org','@type':'CollectionPage',name:'Abhishek Gola — Projects',about:{'@type':'SoftwareSourceCode',name:'calibsense',codeRepository:'https://github.com/calibsense/calibsense',programmingLanguage:'Python',author:{'@type':'Person',name:'Abhishek Gola'},license:'https://www.gnu.org/licenses/agpl-3.0.html'}}}><div id="top"></div><section class="page-intro container"><span class="eyebrow">PROJECTS / FROM THEORY TO TOOLS</span><h1>Built to answer<br/><span class="blue-text">real questions.</span></h1><p>Public engineering work in calibration, measurement, and inference performance. With the source, assumptions, and limitations close at hand.</p></section><section class="page-content container projects-content"><article class="project-feature"><div class="project-visual"><svg viewBox="0 0 400 290" role="img" aria-label="Conceptual calibration uncertainty propagation from camera parameters to a task-space confidence region"><defs><pattern id="dots" width="20" height="20" patternUnits="userSpaceOnUse"><circle cx="1" cy="1" r="1" fill="#cdd4df"/></pattern></defs><rect width="400" height="290" fill="url(#dots)"/><path d="M65 145 300 55 300 235Z" fill="#0071e3" fill-opacity=".04" stroke="#afc5df" stroke-dasharray="4 5"/><rect x="40" y="120" width="52" height="50" rx="10" fill="white" stroke="#839ab6"/><circle cx="68" cy="145" r="15" stroke="#0071e3" fill="#e8f1fc"/><path d="M300 45v200M200 145h160" stroke="#a9b7c8"/><ellipse cx="300" cy="145" rx="34" ry="66" fill="#0071e3" fill-opacity=".08" stroke="#0071e3"/><ellipse cx="300" cy="145" rx="18" ry="40" fill="none" stroke="#0071e3" stroke-dasharray="3 4"/><circle cx="300" cy="145" r="4" fill="#0071e3"/><g font-family="monospace" font-size="10" fill="#6e6e73"><text x="35" y="198">CAMERA</text><text x="240" y="267">TASK-SPACE ERROR</text><text x="148" y="80">PROPAGATE Σ</text></g></svg></div><div class="project-copy"><span class="eyebrow">01 / CALIBRATION & MEASUREMENT</span><h2>calibsense<span class="blue-text">.</span></h2><p>Does your calibration support the measurement you need? A low reprojection error alone cannot answer that question.</p><p>Created by Abhishek, calibsense carries calibration uncertainty into task space and diagnoses when a forecast is not defensible.</p><div class="tags"><span>Python</span><span>OpenCV</span><span>Uncertainty</span><span>AGPL-3.0</span></div><div class="source-actions"><a class="button primary" href="https://github.com/calibsense/calibsense">Source & documentation ↗</a><a class="text-link" href="https://pypi.org/project/calibsense/">PyPI ↗</a></div></div></article><div class="prose project-prose"><h2>From a fit to a decision.</h2><div class="architecture" role="img" aria-label="Calibration detections flow through a fit, covariance diagnosis, task-space propagation, and an audit report"><span>Detections + calibration</span><i>→</i><span>Fit & covariance</span><i>→</i><span>Diagnose & propagate</span><i>→</i><span>JSON / HTML / PDF</span></div><p>The public implementation retains parameter covariance and checks identifiability before reporting task-space uncertainty. Reports expose warnings rather than treating every fitted model as trustworthy.</p><p><strong>Limits:</strong> the documented scope is one camera. Stereo tasks take the baseline as exact; board geometry is assumed exact unless its tolerance is supplied. Real-world accuracy therefore depends on assumptions outside the fitted random-error model. See the <a href="https://github.com/calibsense/calibsense#scope">documented scope</a> before using a forecast.</p></div><article class="project-detail"><span class="eyebrow">02 / INFERENCE BENCHMARKING</span><h2>COOL-Benchmark</h2><p>A public benchmark repository for the Cloud Optimized OpenCV Library on AWS Graviton. The useful artifact is a reproducible workload and its setup, rather than an isolated speedup claim. This is collaborative OpenCV work; repository authorship and contribution history remain the source of credit.</p><div class="architecture" aria-label="Benchmark workflow"><span>Workload</span><i>→</i><span>OpenCV build</span><i>→</i><span>Graviton execution</span><i>→</i><span>Measured results</span></div><p>Results depend on instance type, build configuration, input and measurement method. No benchmark was rerun for this site.</p><div class="source-actions"><a class="button outline" href="https://github.com/opencv/COOL-Benchmark">Repository & instructions ↗</a><a class="text-link" href="/writing/">Related AWS publication →</a></div></article><p class="note">Professional reconstruction and localization work is described only where public disclosure is established. No proprietary captures, employer systems, or unsupported performance results are reproduced.</p></section></Layout>
